[Music]  besides being  a designer i've also been an educator  for many years  you can consider me a modern day  polymath  [Music]  i don't really understand what design  meant  then but the visuals were very  attractive to me  so i ended up studying architecture in  the university  and i actually started my first fencing  in school and i sold it for one dollar  to all my friends  so i think that really sparked my  interest  in publishing and eventually led me into  the road of  entrepreneurship and design  each was started in 1999 at that point  of time there were no  platforms for young designers to  showcase their works and talents so i  wanted to create  ish as a platform to showcase local  talents  local designs to give them that platform  to shine  when i started my nd and 15 minutes it  was with the same vision of providing  a creative platform for singapore  designers and creatives  to have a space to showcase their talent  this is my way of  kind of like contributing to the  singapore design ecosystem  and also my personal way of contributing  to the design scene  over the years i've come to reflect that  my practice  is a lot about documentation and  archival  of the singapore design scene and i hope  to continue this  documentation and archiver on an online  platform called studio sml  and this website will document all young  and old designers  of all disciplines before they shine and  before they die  i've dedicated my life to being a  designer and educator  winning the pda means that i'll continue  to do the same  but also to serve as an advocate and  ambassador for the design industry  i'm grateful for the opportunity that i  have  to mentor many young designers and to  share my knowledge over the years  and for me i will always bear in mind  that the first role of a designer is to  serve  you

